<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37419" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praecīsĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		praecido. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A cutting off</i> (post - Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genitalium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 1, p. 106, 12</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, concr., <i>the piece
				cut off</i>, <i>a cut</i>, <i>cutting</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tignorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 4,
					2</span></i>
			; <i>absol.</i>, <i><span class="en">id. 5,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In rhetoric, <i>a breaking off abruptly</i>, =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποσιώπησις</span>,
					<i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 4, 30,
			41</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>An overreaching</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">finis praecisionis tuae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Jer. 51, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
